Guard against a select2 widget that has no config attached.

https://www.drupal.org/project/select2/issues/3279387

An element can carry the .select2-widget class without ever getting its
data-select2-config attribute, and then the very next line throws. Everything
after it in Drupal.behaviors is abandoned, so a single such element takes the
rest of the page's JavaScript down with it.

The issue proposes wrapping the whole body in `if (config)`. This does the same
thing by leaving early instead, which keeps the patch to four lines and lets it
survive the upstream edits that broke the previous version of it.

--- a/js/select2.js
+++ b/js/select2.js
@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@
     attach: function (context) {
       $(once('select2-init', '.select2-widget', context)).each(function () {
         var config = $(this).data('select2-config');
+        if (!config) {
+          return;
+        }
+
